WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.883
- What's up y'all?

00:00:00.883 --> 00:00:02.520
I'm Joelle and for the next week,

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.250
I am going to attempt to eat

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.950
like the incredible, iconic, sensational

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.700
Korean boy band BTS.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.130
My friend Jasmine over on
Tasty recently made a video

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.170
detailing how to make one of
each member's favorite dishes,

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:16.630
so I was inspired to
deep dive even further

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:20.160
into the lives of seven
of my favorite humans

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.740
and try to eat some of
their favorite foods

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:24.410
throughout the week, dedicating
one day to each member.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:26.080
If I've learned anything
from the many hours

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.060
of behind the scenes footage
and live streams of them

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.150
I've watched, it's that they
are hard workers and big eaters

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.100
so I need to go do some grocery shopping

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.597
and I'll see y'all soon.

00:00:34.597 --> 00:00:37.097
(light music)

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.630
It only felt right to
start out with RM's day,

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:44.630
who is kinda seen as BTS's leader.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.720
He is a crazy talented rapper.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.300
I thought I would start out the day

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.080
with a lovely Korean pastry.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.300
This one is filled with sweet bean paste.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.850
In a Vlive, Jimin and RM
were making Dalgona coffee

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.380
and they were trying to whip it by hand

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:01.240
to varying degrees of success,
so I decided to make my own.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.073
Mm.

00:01:02.073 --> 00:01:04.350
Whenever my family gets
these, they disappear so fast.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:05.183
So good!

00:01:05.183 --> 00:01:08.700
Why don't we kick off the
day with our BTS fun fact?

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.990
BTS stands for Bangtan Sonyeondan,

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:14.350
which translates in English
to Bulletproof Boy Scouts,

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.440
and it's meant to symbolize
how the group is immune

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.360
to the stereotypes,
assumptions and critiques

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.900
about young people today.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.265
I am so excited for
lunch because apparently,

00:01:23.265 --> 00:01:27.070
RM loves kalguksu, which is
also one of my favorite dishes.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:29.610
It is Korean knife-cut noodle soup.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.720
Look at all the noodles.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.360
I just splattered on my face.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.550
When you order this at
restaurants in Korea,

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:37.630
a lot of times, they'll bring it to you

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.300
in a huge bowl for the table.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.900
I always reach a midday
slump around three-ish,

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.320
so it's a good time for
me to have my snack.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.580
I know that RM is happy to eat gummy bears

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:51.520
at all hours of the day.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.680
I think there was an episode
of one of their reality shows

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.190
where he was literally eating gummy bears

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:56.023
first thing in the morning.

00:01:56.023 --> 00:01:58.180
I don't think I could
do that to my stomach,

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.310
but as an afternoon treat, why not?

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:04.947
So the last meal for RM's day
is just as iconic as he is

00:02:04.947 --> 00:02:09.030
and that is samgyeopsal, which
is Korean grilled pork belly.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:11.760
It's really common to get at
any Korean barbecue place,

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.240
served with rice, normally
to wrap in red leaf lettuce

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.590
or kkaennip, which is perilla leaf.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:19.280
And you always have it with banchan,

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.290
which is all the little
Korean side dishes.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:24.410
You eat it all together and
it is absolutely delicious.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.810
But if you wanna be really pro with it,

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:28.280
you would take your leaf, take your meat.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.080
One of my favorite things
that I learned about RM

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.570
is that he taught himself English

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:34.630
through watching reruns of "Friends".

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.260
When I think about how
many hours of K-drama

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:40.010
or anime I've watched with
retaining next to zero

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.790
Korean or Japanese,
that's really impressive.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:43.790
Good for you, man!

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:44.740
Proud of you.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.190
Jimin is one of the group's vocalists

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:49.570
and he is a beautiful
dancer, and he's also known

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:51.440
for just having the sweetest little face,

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.230
which has given him the nickname Mochi,

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:55.350
which I feel like is very fitting.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.640
Starting out super simple,

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.670
I think it was in a
Buzzfeed video actually,

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.740
that Jimin said that he
really likes eating fruit,

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.870
so I just made myself a
cute little fruit platter.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.050
Jimin said that he loves
meat, particularly beef,

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:06.770
so I wanted to make some bulgogi,

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.720
which is really just
marinated Korean beef.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.660
But I didn't think it'd
be enough on its own,

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.840
so I combined it in some bibimbap,

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.880
which is a Korean dish of mixed
rice with a lot of veggies,

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.400
meat, and ideally topped
with a sunny side up egg

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.380
and mixed in with a ton of gochujang.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.720
Before I devour this entire thing,

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.980
our BTS fun fact of the day

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.260
is that BTS is the first Kpop group

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:30.870
to ever get their own
custom Twitter emojis.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:34.680
For me growing up, Kpop
was not seen as cool,

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.170
so the fact that Twitter
has acknowledged BTS

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.260
with their own custom
emojis, I feel just speaks

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.850
to the global reach of
BTS and how awesome it is

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:45.370
that nowadays, people all over
the world can listen to Kpop

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:46.570
and really enjoy it.

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.660
So it is finally dinner time

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.290
and one of Jimin's favorites
that is also a Korean staple

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.210
is kimchi jjigae, which
is just a kimchi stew.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.480
I figured since Jimin is a meat lover,

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:00.100
I would make mine with pork belly.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.100
Apparently, Jimin can't
handle spice super well,

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.780
even though he likes it,
which is very similar to me,

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.911
so I always have my rice on standby.

00:04:07.911 --> 00:04:08.744
Hot.

00:04:08.744 --> 00:04:09.577
(Joelle laughs)

00:04:09.577 --> 00:04:10.410
Mm, so good.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:12.930
- Hot.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:16.710
- Alrighty, good morning
y'all and happy J-Hope day.

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:19.920
J-Hope is a literal ray of sunshine

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.440
and he's one of the group's
main rappers and dancers.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:26.130
So graceful, but then also
hits so hard when he dances.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.130
But in terms of taste, he
says that he really likes

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:30.739
traditional Korean foods,
so I'm starting off my day

00:04:30.739 --> 00:04:33.640
with some fresh kimbap that
I just got from the market.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.760
It's a mixture of veggies,
sometimes some meat.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.670
This one has fish cake with rice

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.210
and wrapped in roasted seaweed.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.320
It's super delicious
and great for on the go.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.153
Mm.

00:04:43.153 --> 00:04:44.596
It's so good because it's just one bite

00:04:44.596 --> 00:04:47.260
of literally everything
you want in a meal.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:48.850
I also feel like I must clarify.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.480
I've seen people refer to
this as sushi on the Internet.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:52.380
It's not sushi.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.800
Kimbap refers to the seaweed.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.700
Kim is the Korean word for that seaweed,

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.710
and then bap is the Korean word for rice.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.590
Another fun find at the grocery store,

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.500
an iced Americano with
little Hobi's face on it.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.880
I actually don't think I've
ever had an iced Americano,

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.940
but I feel like in every single K-drama,

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.350
whenever anyone's at a coffee shop,

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:11.230
someone orders an iced Americano.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:13.280
Ooh, it's not bitter at all.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:16.310
Another traditional dish that
I saw J-Hope really enjoying

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:20.020
on a Vlive is kimchi bokkeumbap,
or kimchi fried rice,

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.760
and I feel like an OG way of
making it includes pork belly,

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.940
of course your kimchi and some veggies

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:26.900
and topping it with a fried egg,

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:29.330
because I'm a firm
believer that a fried egg

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.710
makes everything look and taste better.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:34.430
Okay y'all, I am not a Tasty chef,

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.020
but I will say this looks pretty fire.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.040
Look at how it jiggles.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.300
This is another one of those dishes

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.970
that's great to make when
you just have a bunch

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:42.330
of leftover stuff in the kitchen,

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:45.613
because you can put anything
you want in your fried rice.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:47.770
Okay.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:49.890
J-Hope is actually the only member of BTS

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.260
that doesn't have his ears pierced,

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:55.280
so hope you all appreciate,
I took out my earrings today

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.450
in honor of J-Hope.

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:58.690
While BTS eats a lot of
traditional Korean foods

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:00.490
while at home, obviously
they're on the road a lot,

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:02.800
and apparently one of their
favorite places to come

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.450
when they're on the
West Coast is In-N-Out,

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:07.330
and I feel like in almost every
interview, J-Hope mentions,

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:10.640
- I love hamburger and Sprite!

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.960
- However, apparently
I didn't do my research

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.890
well enough though, because
when I came to In-N-Out,

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.608
they said they don't serve Sprite.

00:06:16.608 --> 00:06:17.810
So I had to get 7 Up.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.370
I'm sorry, J-Hope, I failed you.

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:21.580
But can I personally taste the difference?

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:22.413
No.

00:06:22.413 --> 00:06:24.890
So I will enjoy it either way.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.970
I'm actually here with my sister too.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:27.930
Woohoo.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:31.140
What do you think of
the J-Hope burger meal?

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.610
- It's just a cheeseburger so it's great.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:37.120
- And today's fun fact is that
BTS almost wasn't called BTS.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.070
They considered the names
Big Kids and Young Nation

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:42.440
before landing on Bangtan Sonyeondan,

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:44.980
so I'm glad that they came to
the consensus that they did.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:47.020
Welcome to V's day.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:49.820
V is one of the main dancers
and vocalists for BTS

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.440
and he's also just generally
known for being a hottie,

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:53.670
which I love for him.

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:56.320
One of his fan-appointed nicknames is CGV,

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:58.490
literally standing for computer graphics V

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:01.890
because they say he's too
attractive to be real.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:04.420
Anyways, I'm starting off the
day with one of V's favorites,

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:07.950
which is apparently japchae,
which is stir-fried noodles.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:08.873
So normally this dish is made

00:07:08.873 --> 00:07:10.850
with sweet potato starch noodles,

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:13.177
which I thought I had but I didn't have.

00:07:13.177 --> 00:07:15.500
I'm actually using rice
vermicelli noodles,

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:16.447
which is not what you're supposed to do,

00:07:16.447 --> 00:07:18.080
but I used the same marinade

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.133
and a lot of the same stir-fried veggies.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:22.850
Mm.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:25.660
I will say it's not bad for
my first try ever making this.

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:26.810
The noodles are actually seasoned

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:28.800
with a little bit of honey or brown sugar,

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.310
so they have a slight sweetness.

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:31.447
Also, some of y'all might be thinking,

00:07:31.447 --> 00:07:33.640
"Why are you eating noodles
first thing in the morning?"

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:36.180
Noodles are always an
appropriate food to eat.

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.310
Fun but very random addition
to today's challenge,

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:40.650
I read that V is a big fan of Gucci.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.430
Kpop groups wear a lot of designer brands

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.400
in performances and in general.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.540
But since V has been particularly vocal

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.210
about his love for the brand,

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:49.709
I asked my friend if I could borrow

00:07:49.709 --> 00:07:52.160
her Gucci belt for today.

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:53.950
If this one thing will help me feel

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:57.370
one step closer to being
that eighth member of BTS,

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:58.830
you know I had to do it.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.620
Okay, so it is now lunchtime

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.200
and I feel like I can't
make a BTS eating video

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.580
without including jajangmyeon,

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.630
which is Korean black bean noodles.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:08.880
There's one very memorable
clip that stays in my mind

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.847
of V having to eat jajangmyeon silently.

00:08:11.847 --> 00:08:14.120
(light music)

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:16.630
The kind he was eating kind of
looked like the instant ones,

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:18.697
Chapagetti, which is one of my favorite

00:08:18.697 --> 00:08:20.240
instant noodle brands,

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:22.600
but I decided I would try
to be fancy and make my own.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.530
Inga actually has a
video up on About to Eat

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.260
showing how she makes
it, so I tried to follow

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:28.390
a rendition of that recipe.

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:29.930
So this is my version.

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:32.340
I'm really excited, I've
never made this before

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:34.163
and it looks and smells bomb.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:39.530
This sauce, I truly feel
like there's no comparison

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:41.250
I could make to an American version.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:43.460
It's so rich and creamy,

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.100
but the flavor's just completely different

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:47.420
from anything I have in any other cuisine.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.680
Ooh, another fun thing I learned about V

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:52.000
is that he actually didn't
plan on coming to audition

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.050
to be a Kpop idol.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:54.540
He came to the auditions with a friend

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:57.190
just to keep him company
and then, lo and behold,

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:58.300
actually turned out to be

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.700
one of the world's biggest pop stars, so.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.290
Dinner time, I'm tired.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:04.150
If you've ever seen BTS in an interview

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:05.640
where they ask where you like to eat

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.630
when you're in the
States, nearly every time,

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:09.800
V will be very enthusiastic

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.070
about one restaurant in particular,

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.630
and that restaurant is Panda Express.

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:15.730
I couldn't find exactly
what V likes to order

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:19.630
when he's there, but Panda
Express actually has tweeted BTS

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:22.130
and they used the hashtag
#OrangeChickenLove,

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:24.840
which made me think, "I
better get orange chicken."

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:27.790
First piece of orange
chicken in years, mm.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.170
Wow, it is so sweet.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.900
As I was watching these interviews

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.380
where V would exclaim his
love for Panda Express,

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:36.161
and then a lot of the times,
interviewers seem confused

00:09:36.161 --> 00:09:38.490
and they'll say something
maybe along the lines of,

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:41.163
- [Interviewer] Okay, came
a long way for Asian food,

00:09:41.163 --> 00:09:43.780
but it's probably not as
good as you get back home.

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:45.910
- To be honest, I've
never met an Asian person

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:48.470
that considers Panda
Express to be Asian food.

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:51.980
It's like Americans
cosplaying Chinese food

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:52.813
with Panda Express.

00:09:52.813 --> 00:09:54.540
It's still delicious in its own way,

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:57.160
but I respectfully would not
consider this Chinese food.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.610
And of course, I couldn't end V's day

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.320
without giving a BTS fact,

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:01.830
and today's fact is that BTS

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:03.850
has broken multiple world records,

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:06.390
and as of this video, their
most recent world record

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:09.660
has been most simultaneous
viewers on a music video

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:12.820
on YouTube Premieres with
their video for "Dynamite".

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:14.350
Suga is one of BTS's rappers,

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:16.670
and is just such a sweet little presence.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.840
Suga has said that one of
his greatest simple pleasures

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:23.100
in life is drinking iced
Americano on an empty stomach,

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.115
so before I eat anything,

00:10:24.115 --> 00:10:27.000
I've made myself an iced Americano.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.440
Okay, I think I might've
made it a little weak,

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.480
but it's not bad.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.570
And for my actual breakfast,
Suga is a big fruit guy.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.960
That's right baby, we're
eating hella tangerines

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:36.890
for breakfast today.

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:38.700
You can find literal compilations

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.650
of Suga just eating tangerines

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:42.640
because he enjoys them so much.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.240
One interesting thing
I learned about Suga,

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:46.120
his name, stage name, Suga,

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.890
is that it doesn't come
from the sweetener.

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:50.240
It's actually from his old position

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:53.130
that he played in basketball,
which was the shooting guard.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.470
Shooting guard, Suga, ha ha.

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:56.580
If there's one thing that I feel

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:58.420
like BTS constantly eats together

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.645
and that they say that
they enjoy together a lot,

00:11:00.645 --> 00:11:03.370
that is fried chicken and beer.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:06.030
There's something about Korean
fried chicken specifically

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:07.120
just hits so different.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:10.340
Oh my gosh, this smells so good!

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:11.220
Mm.

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:14.440
If you've never had Korean fried
chicken, this is your sign.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:15.930
Given that Suga's a big meat eater,

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:17.240
I figured that tonight
was an appropriate night

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:20.450
to have galbi, which are
Korean marinated short ribs.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.600
Jasmine has a great recipe
for this y'all can follow,

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:24.900
however I just got mine pre-marinated

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:26.460
from the Korean grocery store.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.100
Even easier to cook and prep.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:31.810
I'm so excited for this,
this smells so incredible.

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:33.290
Mm.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:34.730
You know what we haven't done yet today?

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:35.563
Our BTS fact.

00:11:35.563 --> 00:11:38.300
Today's fact is that unlike
a lot of other Kpop groups,

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.410
BTS actually writes their own songs,

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:41.310
and from my understanding,

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:43.060
it's generally a collaborative effort.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:44.870
However, Suga has been known to say

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.470
that he is an extremely
prolific songwriter

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:50.070
being able to write
songs in one to two days,

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:52.600
which literally just blows my mind.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:55.340
Okay, the day has finally
come for Jin's day.

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:56.173
I'm so excited

00:11:56.173 --> 00:11:58.870
because Jin is kind of the
notorious eater of BTS.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:01.850
He made his own mukbang
eating show called Eat Jin

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:05.450
where he just bodies the most
ridiculous volumes of food

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:06.640
and I love that for him.

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:08.450
He's also one of the main
vocalists for the group,

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.920
and I think he has an
incredible sense of humor.

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:13.670
Today's breakfast, I have
to admit, I cannot guarantee

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:16.990
is one of Jin's favorite foods,
but it's very Jin inspired.

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:18.410
One of his philosophies around food

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:19.840
that he mentioned in an Eat Jin episode

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:22.080
was that ramen seasoning,
the little packet,

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:23.730
makes everything taste good.

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:26.990
So I figured I would try
to make scrambled eggs

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:29.490
seasoned with ramen seasoning.

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:32.769
My eggs do smell a little
bit like seafood ramen,

00:12:32.769 --> 00:12:34.360
which is interesting.

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:36.603
But it's also making my mouth water.

00:12:37.856 --> 00:12:40.330
Oh my gosh, it's not bad.

00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:42.920
It tastes like when you
put an egg in your ramen

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:46.130
and you scramble it in your
soup, it tastes like that egg.

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:48.290
I think we can deduce that Jin was correct

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:52.980
in that ramen seasoning does
make things taste really good.

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:56.130
One of my favorite things
to watch Jin eat is noodles,

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:58.250
so I decided to make one
of his apparent favorites,

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.550
and that is naengmyeon, which
is my childhood favorite.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:02.880
It is a cold buckwheat noodle soup

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.290
and it's super chewy and satisfying.

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:06.920
You can make it from
scratch with the noodles

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:08.955
and then a beef based broth.

00:13:08.955 --> 00:13:11.740
I just decided to get
another instant packet,

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:14.540
which is super easy to
make, very convenient

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:17.010
and just as satisfying in my opinion.

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:19.550
I like to top mine with some
veggies and a boiled egg.

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:21.610
It's best on a very hot summer day

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.660
and it's just super refreshing.

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:26.050
Jin can probably shove it
in his mouth all at once

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:28.240
the volume of noodles I
have in my entire bowl.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:29.670
Let's see how closely I can imitate

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:31.393
how Jin takes a giant bite.

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:33.840
Oh.

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:35.850
Okay, I immediately decided
I don't like shoving

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:37.720
that many noodles in
my mouth like Jin does,

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:40.090
but it's very impressive
that he can do it.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:42.740
I will also say, one of my
favorite things about Jin,

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:44.850
just as a person, because
we know each other so well,

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:48.100
is that one minute he can be
shoving noodles into his mouth

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:49.610
like his life depends on it,

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:52.490
and then he'll go into an
interview and introduce himself.

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:53.660
- Hello I'm Jin.

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:55.690
I'm Worldwide Handsome.

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.890
- Given that he was
scouted for his good looks,

00:13:57.890 --> 00:13:58.780
go off, Jin.

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.540
But I would love to have
that level of confidence.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:02.530
So Jin strikes me as a very fancy man

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:05.250
because he says that one of
his favorite foods is lobster.

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:08.990
Class, I'm sitting in my
family's fancy dining room today.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:11.950
I know Jin has also
said that he loves steak

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.520
and he eats three steaks a day.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:14.847
As much as I wanted to do that,

00:14:14.847 --> 00:14:17.140
I thought that I'd been
doing a lot of beef already,

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:19.880
so I decided to go with lobster
as our more exciting option.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:23.100
I wasn't exactly sure how he
likes his lobster prepared,

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:25.210
so I was looking online and
there's a type of lobster

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:28.540
that is prepared and served as
regular street food in Korea.

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:30.903
It's seasoned with gochujang
and topped with cheese.

00:14:30.903 --> 00:14:34.350
It looked super delicious so I
tried my hand at making that.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.423
Very nervous to see how it tastes.

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:40.100
The cheese feels weirdly placed.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:42.510
I feel like it'd be better
almost without the cheese.

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:45.200
It's probably my fault because
I used Gouda and cheddar

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:47.148
instead of Gouda and mozzarella, but.

00:14:47.148 --> 00:14:49.170
Little funky, but it's still good.

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:50.190
I'm gonna eat the whole thing.

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:53.780
And today's fun fact is
that BTS's logo since 2017

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:55.650
is made up of two trapezoids.

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:59.130
It's meant to represent
two doors opening outwards.

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:01.830
And then on the other
hand, the logo for ARMY,

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:04.650
BTS's fan base, is those
trapezoids reversed,

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:07.010
so it looks like the
doors are opening inwards.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.030
And those two together
are supposed to represent

00:15:09.030 --> 00:15:12.320
BTS and ARMY coming together as one,

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:15.470
which I think is so
lovely and poetic of them.

00:15:16.762 --> 00:15:17.750
- Pretty good.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:18.996
- [Joelle] Okay, what
would we rate it out of 10?

00:15:18.996 --> 00:15:19.829
- That is pretty good.

00:15:19.829 --> 00:15:21.322
I would say eight.

00:15:21.322 --> 00:15:22.460
- Nice!

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:24.000
It is Jungkook day!

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:26.360
He's a dancer and vocalist for the group,

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:28.040
and he's also the youngest.

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:30.040
Listen, they call him the Golden Maknae

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:32.310
because he's good at everything,

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:34.480
and for that, we have to stan.

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:36.710
Apparently, he said
that he's a big carb fan

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:39.287
and I've seen in a lot of
behind the scenes clips

00:15:39.287 --> 00:15:42.330
that he likes bananas and peanut butter.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:43.780
He made himself this delicious looking

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:46.130
peanut butter Nutella banana toast,

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:47.237
and when I saw that, I was like,

00:15:47.237 --> 00:15:49.317
"Oh my gosh, that's what I
used to have after school

00:15:49.317 --> 00:15:51.410
"when I was a little kid as a snack",

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:52.793
so I had to make it.

00:15:54.131 --> 00:15:55.730
A+ for Jungkook's breakfast.

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:57.850
Given that Jungkook's a carb lover,

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:59.490
I feel like I had to make tteokbokki,

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:01.390
which is just a classic Korean dish.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:03.640
It's literally spicy rice cakes

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:05.010
that are all stewed together.

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:07.146
Little bit of fish cakes,
I like to add some veggies

00:16:07.146 --> 00:16:09.270
and in all the eating compilations,

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:10.390
Jungkook's always eating noodles,

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:12.160
so I had to add some ramen.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:14.220
It's a really common pairing in Korea

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:16.350
when you get tteokbokki,
you can add ramen noodles,

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:19.610
you can add cheese on top,
all these fun fixings.

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:21.160
So that's what I tried to make.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.630
Oh, pretty good.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:25.790
Hey, it's pretty good.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:26.623
My sister.

00:16:26.623 --> 00:16:27.500
There's a lot of different
flavors going on.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.750
We've got spice, we've
got all this seafood,

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:31.670
we've got the sweetness.

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:33.760
Another random fun fact
I learned about Jungkook

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:36.390
is that he actually is
a big fan of body art.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:39.890
He has I think over 11 tattoos.

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:43.580
I wanted to emulate Jungkook,
so I got a temporary tattoo,

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.630
which my family will be
much more on board with.

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:49.220
I got this tiger one though
because Siberian tigers

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:51.570
are the national animal of Korea.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.060
I am honestly really bummed,

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:56.400
this is my last BTS inspired meal.

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:59.070
I know Jungkook likes pizza, I like pizza,

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:00.100
so we're having pizza.

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:03.140
In clips of BTS having a
little pizza party together,

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:06.640
I know RM mentioned something
about a supreme pizza,

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:09.250
so I figured a supreme
pizza was the way to go.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:11.350
Pizza in Korea is actually super bomb.

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:13.810
You can get things like
sweet potato crust,

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:15.820
which sounds weird I think to Americans

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:18.720
but it's really good, and just
a lot of different toppings

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:20.090
that you wouldn't find in the States.

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:21.060
As I'm enjoying this,

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:24.150
might as well share our
final BTS fact of this video,

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:28.100
and that is in 2018, BTS's
album "Love Yourself: Tear"

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:32.220
was the first Kpop album to
ever top the Billboard 200.

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:34.220
Dinner is over, I have my dessert.

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:37.030
I know that Jungkook
is a big fan of sweets,

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:40.500
especially cookies, so I'm
eating Oreos and drinking milk

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:41.820
out of a bowl I think.

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:45.080
It also seemed appropriate
because Jungkook's character

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.590
that he made in collaboration
with Line Friends,

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:49.940
the BT21 line, is literally named Cooky,

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:52.850
so gotta end my week with some cookies.

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:54.488
And I'm looking back at the photos

00:17:54.488 --> 00:17:56.760
of all the different meals I had

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.850
and they all look so good,

00:17:58.850 --> 00:18:00.720
but there could only be one winner.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.910
One ultimate day from
this eating like BTS week,

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:07.680
and my favorite day will
probably have to be Suga's day,

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:09.890
because ever since that
day, I have been in love

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:12.240
with iced Americanos and tangerines,

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:15.320
and you really can't beat
Korean fried chicken.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:18.720
Though I will say, RM's
day with the kalguksu,

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:19.920
very close second.

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:21.240
But please let me know which day

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:22.470
you would have liked to eat,

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:24.340
which BTS member would you like to share

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:25.510
a day of meals with?

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:28.083
And before you go, oh my gosh,
wait, you dropped something.

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:30.327
Bye.

00:18:30.327 --> 00:18:32.827
(light music)

